## Reduced UI corner rounding to minimum (almost square)
================================================================================

Context: The UI had heavily rounded corners across surfaces, including 14px cards,
10px controls/inputs/buttons, 14px submenu dropdowns with 9px rounded items, and
rounded pills. The user requested reducing all rounded boxes (submenus, pages,
cards, modals, inputs, and controls) to the minimum (almost a square).

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/css/main.css
   - Reduced shared radii tokens: `--db-radius-sm: 2px`, `--db-radius-md: 2px`,
     `--db-radius-lg: 2px`, with `--db-radius-control`, `--db-radius-card`, and
     `--db-radius-chip` all resolving to 2px.
   - Added Bootstrap CSS variable overrides in `:root` (`--bs-border-radius: 2px`,
     `--bs-border-radius-sm: 2px`, `--bs-border-radius-lg: 2px`,
     `--bs-card-border-radius: 2px`, `--bs-modal-border-radius: 2px`,
     `--bs-dropdown-border-radius: 2px`, `--bs-btn-border-radius: 2px`,
