================================================================================
## Explicit error message when listing Genie Pages (Knowledge Pages) fails
================================================================================

Context: Context → Pages search showed only "List Knowledge Pages failed" when
Databricks refused the request (e.g. missing permissions). The HTTP status and
the Databricks reason were only in `detail`, which the global handler strips
outside debug mode, so users could not tell the cause.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/KnowledgePageService.py
   - `list_pages` catches `requests.RequestException` and raises an
     `InfrastructureError` built by the new `_list_error` helper.
   - `_list_error` names the cause: 401 (authentication), 403 (permission
     denied, ask a workspace admin), 404 (API not available / Genie Pages not
     enabled), 429 (rate limited), 5xx (Databricks unavailable); other statuses
     get a generic refusal. Appends the HTTP status and the clipped Databricks
     error message. Connection/timeout errors get "Could not reach Databricks".
   - Raw request error stays in `detail` for debug mode.
2. tests/units/core/test_knowledge_pages.py
   - 403 names the missing permission and includes the Databricks message.
   - Connection error gives an explicit "Could not reach Databricks" message.

